WEBVTT

00:05.800 --> 00:10.810
Ratio and proportion is what allows us to compare the value of two things, which is something we do

00:10.810 --> 00:11.680
every day.

00:11.770 --> 00:18.250
Think about the price per gallon of gas or the number of students per classroom, or even the number

00:18.250 --> 00:19.930
of pets per household.

00:20.410 --> 00:25.630
If you remember nothing else from this course, try to remember the concepts from this ratio and proportion

00:25.630 --> 00:26.230
lesson.

00:26.500 --> 00:29.570
Even if you don't end up using advanced math in your daily life.

00:29.590 --> 00:32.860
You can absolutely use ratio and proportion.

00:33.280 --> 00:38.050
We'll start by introducing the concept of ratio and proportion, and then naturally we'll look at some

00:38.050 --> 00:39.640
real world applications.
